From: MythologyKombat local launcher patch set (D19, T3.12)
Subject: [PATCH 0004] PLAYER card: more room under the Analog / D-Pad selector

Issue (design item 4; work/screens/shot_230017.png): the Analog / D-Pad row
  (28 px buttons) is followed by only a 6 px Dummy before the 40 px Keyboard
  combo, so the two rows look glued together.

Fix: the gap under the selector goes from 6 to 12 logical px. The extra height
  is absorbed by patch 0001 (controller art shrinks when the column would
  overflow), so it does not cost a scrollbar.

Verified: partly. The change is visible in the captures, but whether this is the
  element the user meant is a judgement call (the gap was 28 px on screen
  already); the user decides.
Upstream candidate: low value; keep local.
---
diff --git a/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp b/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp
index 2e6eb73..e7d8ea5 100644
--- a/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp
+++ b/src/common/backends/imgui/launcher_imgui.cpp
@@ -3487,7 +3487,9 @@ void draw_player_panel(LauncherModel* m, const LauncherTheme& th, int p, float w
     // is user-selectable (not locked to a single mode).
     if (m->pad_mode_supported && m->pad_mode_selectable) {
         pad_mode_selector(m, th, p, cw);
-        ImGui::Dummy(ImVec2(0, px(6)));
+        // 12, not 6: the 28 px Analog / D-Pad buttons sat a hand's width above
+        // the 40 px source combo and read as part of it.
+        ImGui::Dummy(ImVec2(0, px(12)));
     }
 
     ImGui::SetNextItemWidth(cw);
